# Reference architectures

<PageMeta level="advanced" time="16 min" prereq={[['Lambda vs Kappa', '/docs/flink/architecture/lambda-vs-kappa']]} />

Six designs you will actually be asked to build. Each is specified the same way, in the
order that matters:

```text
Requirement → Topology → Time semantics → State profile →
Checkpoint strategy → Sink strategy → Failure handling → Scaling → Observability
```

The template itself is the transferable part. If you can fill it in for a new
requirement, you can design a Flink system.

---

## 1. Real-time clickstream analytics

**Requirement:** page and product metrics per minute, visible within 30 seconds,
reproducible for finance.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    W[Web / mobile SDK] --> G[Ingest gateway<br/>stamps event_time]
    G --> K[(Kafka: clicks<br/>keyed by user_id)]
    K --> F["Flink<br/>tumbling 1-min windows"]
    F --> U[(upsert-kafka: metrics)]
    F --> L[(Iceberg: raw clicks)]
    U --> D[Dashboard]
    L --> A[Ad-hoc SQL]
```

| Dimension | Decision |
| --- | --- |
| **Time** | Event time. Stamped at the **gateway**, not the client — client clocks cannot be trusted. Bound at p99 measured lateness, typically 10–30s. |
| **State** | Small: one accumulator per (page, window). Tumbling only — resist sliding windows for dashboards. |
| **Checkpoints** | 60s, aligned with a 30s timeout. State is small, so duration is dominated by nothing in particular. |
| **Sinks** | `upsert-kafka` keyed on `(window_start, page)` so allowed-lateness re-fires become updates. Plus a raw Iceberg landing table for everything else. |
| **Failure** | Standard restore. Metrics are idempotent by key, so replay is harmless. |
| **Scaling** | Source parallelism = partition count. Downstream driven by CPU. Key skew is unlikely on `page`. |
| **Observe** | Watermark lag, late-record count, consumer lag. |

<Callout type="prod">

Stamping event time at a gateway you control, rather than trusting the client, removes an
entire class of incident: future-dated timestamps that poison the watermark. Keep the
client's timestamp as a separate field for analysis, and use the gateway's for
processing.

</Callout>

